 "text": "A Hawaiian bay disappeared in less than a week.\n\nKapoho Bay. March 2018.\n\nThen, on May 3rd, the ground under a neighborhood split open.\n\nTwenty-four fissures.\n\nFrom orbit, Landsat's infrared picked up the heat.\n\nOne vent sent lava all the way to the ocean.\n\nIt reached Kapoho Bay on June 3rd. By June 7th, the bay was gone.\n\nNearly fourteen square miles of lava. Over eighteen hundred structures destroyed.\n\nMeanwhile, as magma drained away, the summit collapsed.\n\nThe caldera floor dropped more than sixteen hundred feet.\n\nHawaii gained eight hundred seventy-five acres of new land.\n\nWho owns it? Not the neighbors. Under a 1977 court ruling, it belongs to the State.",
 "text_sha256": "6152a7ebc59744521858b73fad475b63285e52ea7a3128c49407a122c5fe976c",
